      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled metformin dose.\n\n- **Daily maximum:** The FDA-labeled limit is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Extended-release is limited to 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Single-dose maximum:** A single dose is usually capped at 1,000 mg. The usual regimens are 500 mg BID\u2013TID or 850 mg BID\u2013TID.\n- **Safety risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day)\n- **500 mg PO TID with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO BID with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **Some other dose**, such as 170 mg, or a different drug or formulation\n\nIf you confirm that 1,700 mg TID is what you want, I can enter it with a note that you verified the dose. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first. Tell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
